course: dictionary
lesson: 938
title: Reading clues: blizzard
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A blizzard is a very bad snowstorm, with heavy snow, strong wind and so much blowing snow that you can hardly see. The words around it give you clues. «In a Canadian blizzard you stay indoors» tells you it is dangerous weather, because people shelter inside.
explain: The sentence «In a blizzard thousands of emperor penguins huddle together and slowly shuffle» gives more clues. Huddling close means they are trying to keep warm. Try your meaning in the sentence: a very bad snowstorm fits well.
explain: The word has a second meaning, so check which one fits. «A blizzard of emails» means a huge amount of emails arriving all at once. Ask yourself: is the sentence about snow, or about a lot of something? The words around it will tell you.
fact: A blizzard is a very bad snowstorm with strong wind, lots of blowing snow and very poor visibility.
fact: Visibility means how far you can see, so in a blizzard you can see very little.
fact: «Blizzard» can also mean a huge amount of something all at once, like «a blizzard of emails».
fact: Blizzards happen in cold places like Canada, the northern USA and mountains, so people stay indoors and keep warm.
fact: A «raging blizzard» means the snow and wind are at their strongest.
exercise: «In a blizzard thousands of emperor penguins huddle together.» What is a blizzard? | *A very bad snowstorm with strong wind and blowing snow | A group of penguins walking to the sea | A warm, sunny day on the beach | A small, quiet pond in the park
exercise: Lia says, «My inbox had a blizzard of emails this morning.» What does blizzard mean here? | *A huge amount of emails all at once | Cold snow falling on the roof | A slow and quiet morning | Emails sent to the wrong person
exercise: «In a Canadian blizzard you stay indoors.» What should you do in a blizzard? | *Stay indoors and keep warm | Go out to play in the snow | Leave the house early, before it starts | Travel fast to get home before dark
test: Which word in «In a blizzard thousands of emperor penguins huddle together» tells you the penguins are staying close for warmth? | thousands | *huddle | emperor | blizzard
test: Which phrase from the lessons means the snow and wind are at their strongest? | *A raging blizzard | Blizzards in Canada | A blizzard of emails | Caught in a blizzard
exam: Why is it a good idea to check a meaning by swapping it into the sentence? | It tells you how to spell the word | It makes the sentence longer | It means you never need a dictionary again | *It shows whether the meaning still makes sense in the sentence
